Thus after we have transport leg assembled and loading authorized, and origin availability locked and confirmed, we can mark origin dispatch ready.

Thus overall flow for each availability:

1. attach_task_profile (to get task profile linked)
2. confirm_candidate_preparedness (makes candidate_prepared)
3. assign_operator_resource
4. activate_origin_node (or destination)
5. load_origin_payload (or load_destination_payload)
6. lock_origin_availability (makes locked+confirmed)
7. (after both sides done) assemble_transport_leg (requires both locked+confirmed, nodes ready)
8. authorize_transport_leg_loading (requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin)
9. mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready (requires origin_availability_locked, confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized)
10. allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate (requires dispatch_ready, candidate_task_profile_linked, dispatch_slot_available)
11. execute_origin_dispatch (or execute_destination_dispatch) to set dispatched and free vehicle and dispatch slot.

